Here's the API design convention for this project (from .claude/rules/api-design.md):

URLs and Resources

- Plural, lowercase, kebab-case: /api/orders, /api/order-items
- No verbs in paths, max one-level nesting: /api/orders/:id/items
- Path params identify resources; query params filter, sort, paginate
- Non-CRUD actions use sub-resource nouns: POST /api/orders/:id/cancellation

HTTP Methods

┌────────┬────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┐
│ Method │            Purpose             │          Idempotent          │
├────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
│ GET    │ Read, no side effects          │ Yes                          │
├────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
│ POST   │ Create or action               │ No (support Idempotency-Key) │
├────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
│ PUT    │ Replace/update resource        │ Yes                          │
├────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
│ PATCH  │ Partial update (new endpoints) │ No guarantee                 │
├────────┼────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
│ DELETE │ Remove                         │ Yes                          │
└────────┴────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┘

Note: Current PUT /api/orders/:id accepts partial bodies—keep this behavior.

Status Codes

- 200 read/update with body | 201 created (include Location header) | 204 delete/empty success
- 400 invalid input | 401 not authenticated | 403 authenticated but not allowed | 404 not found | 409 conflict
- Never return 200 with error body or 500 for client mistakes

Response Format

Single resource:
{ "id": "...", "customerId": "...", "amount": 1500, "status": "pending" }

List (with pagination):
{ "data": [...], "pagination": { "limit": 20, "nextCursor": "abc" } }

Error (all errors use this shape):
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Invalid request body",
    "details": [{ "path": "amount", "message": "Must be positive" }]
  }
}

Validation & Data Types

- Zod-parse body, params, query with .strict() (rejects unknown fields)
- Money: integer cents, never floats
- IDs: server-generated UUIDs
- Timestamps: ISO 8601 UTC (2026-09-30T10:15:00.000Z)
- Bound every input (max lengths, min/max numbers)

Security

- Identity from auth token only, never from request body
- Every read/update/delete checks caller owns the resource (return 404 for other users' resources)
- No sensitive data in URLs; rate limit all routes (stricter on writes)

New Endpoint Checklist

1. Path, method, status codes match rules
2. Zod schemas with .strict() and bounds
3. Standard error shape + error middleware
4. Pagination/filters/sorts allowlisted (if applicable)
5. Ownership check (if auth exists)
6. Tests: success, 400, 404, 401/403